f boxes and  unpackaging experiences when a new  product arrives at a customer's door  it's very important to a brand and to a  company and that customer enjoys the  unboxing experience it's smooth it's  perfect and it's clean it makes them  really enjoy the product a little bit  more and it makes them feel like they've  been thought about the added benefit in  2019 of creating a unique product with a  unique  boxing experience is the fact that your  customers may potentially post this  product online social media nowadays is  a number one key selling point to sell  anything so when a customer posts a  picture of their brand new watch for  example they're going to show their  friends potentially 100 500 500 thousand  people that you've never had access to  before one photo like this and one share  like this can be worked more than  spending tens of thousands of dollars  online on Facebook marketing and  Instagram marketing because these people  are very interested in their friends and  their family and what they're doing and  what they're spending their money on now  if you're new to this channel and have  no idea about my past experience in  business one of the companies I've  created in the past is called wild  watches there's a link in the  description if you want to check it out  and see what I do for a living  so far there's been two collections  launched and two completely different  unboxing experiences the first  collection featured a unique white box  that created an unboxing experience  different to anything on the market at  the time launched the intention of this  unboxing experience was to create  something different and unique something  a customer would remember and really  enjoy unboxing again and again so being  the first collection that I ever  launched I wanted this box to be  something special and I wanted the  customer to take a little bit of time to  enjoy all the details and the processes  behind creating something like a watch a  single leaflet at the bottom depicted  how a customer could easily set up their  watching four simple steps it really  created a unique experience for them and  it wasn't just grab the watch out of the  box put her on and forget about it it's  just another watch this unboxing  experience encourage the customer to put  together to watch and understand that  all the straps and all the combinations  were completely interchangeable if this  was by any chance missed on the website  or it wasn't conveyed properly the  customer really understood straight away  when they unboxed his products the  second collection was called the  midnight collection and obviously the  midnight collection had to come in a  black box so the reasoning behind this  packaging here was the fact that the  second collection was really about  creating a gift to the customer  themselves they had provided myself and  others the opportunity to continue a  dream that was never before possible  unlike the original collection the  midnight collection did come assembled  now the reason behind this was to really  encourage the customers  to understand more so about the brand  and the watch itself so inside the  packaging a little unique booklet was  created just showing pictographic images  of how the watch could be assembled how  it could be adjusted and how anything  could be changed on the timepiece itself  now having a unique box and a unique  product unpackage comes with its pros  and cons being a small company that  doesn't produce millions and millions of  products every single week there are  some drawbacks to creating a unique box  that takes time and effort by the  company to produce so for example the  midnight collection box which is a  smooth transitional 2-piece unit costs  about $10 to make for most people  something like this would be just thrown  into the bin and completely forgotten  about but others it would have been the  key difference between purchasing one of  our watches and somebody else's a little  piece of advice that I've learned over  the years is if you're creating a unique  unboxing experience make sure you set  some time aside to create and develop  this box itself the product can take six  to twelve months to create but the box  itself can again take something like  three to six months to create on top of  that as you begin developing your  product and things change parts change  it becomes bigger and smaller the boxes  have to adjust in size and shape to suit  as well so make sure you request the  sample of every single box that you  create before you go to for production  if you're thinking about creating your  very own product packaging and your very  own unique product there's multiple ways  to think about it products packaging  itself if you're creating a sleek  stylish product that's very thin and  narrow maybe consider the box to be as  still as possible otherwise if you're  creating something that's extravagant  and very expensive take a look at  something like the Samsung Galaxy fold  the box comes in a box in a box in a box  there's more and more on packaging and  different experiences inside the one  unit considering the number of products  that Samsung has pushed out for this  product the boxes probably didn't cost  them that much but they still would have  been upwards of $50 just in the single  unboxing experience however it does  create a very luxurious feel and if  that's a product that you're selling  upwards of $2000 well maybe it's  something you can sit up because the  customer isn't going to be very happy if  the $2000 product comes in a very basic  cardboard box and it feels like they're  being chipped out and that's all I have  for you guys today on unboxing and the  unbox  experience if there's anything you'd  like to know more about today's topic  make sure you drop a comment down below  otherwise smash that subscribe button  20-19 style I'll see you next Monday

